[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186203943 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/id #uuid "e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/math-academy-id "q-225260" :question/problem "**Fully** factor the following trinomial.\n\n$-12{a}^{2}-6a+6=$\n{{field-1}}$(a\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$)($\n{{field-3}}\n$a\\,-1)$" :question/worked-solution "We need to factor the following expression:\n\n$$\n-12{a}^{2}-6a+6\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all the terms have a common factor of $-6.$ So, we can simplify the calculation by first factoring out $-6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(2{a}^{2}+a-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the trinomial $2{a}^{2}+a-1$ in parentheses. To do this, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant (which is $2\\times (-1)=-2$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient (which is $1$).\n\nThe factor pairs of $-2$ are\n\n$$\n(1,-2),\\,(-1,2).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-1,2)$ add to $1:$ \n\n$$\n-1+2=1\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-a+2a,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}^{2}+a-1 & = \\\\ 2{a}^{2}-a+2a-1 & = \\\\ (2{a}^{2}-a)+(2a-1) & = \\\\ a(2a-1)+(2a-1) & = \\\\ (a+1)(2a-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original trinomial factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12{a}^{2}-6a+6 & = \\\\ -6(2{a}^{2}+a-1) & = \\\\ -6(a+1)(2a-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" "answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" "answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer/id #uuid "b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/id #uuid "417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer-field/choices ["answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer/id #uuid "592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/id #uuid "97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer/id #uuid "fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054604 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/id #uuid "03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/math-academy-id "q-338386" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Applying the root rule, we get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3(0)^{2}+6(0)+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0+0+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{9}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{729} \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/id #uuid "b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer/id #uuid "fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "27" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186115323 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/id #uuid "7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-76083" :question/problem "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $3\\le 4x+7\\le 19$ or $6x+8<2?$" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $3\\le 4x+7\\le 19:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & \\le 4x+7\\le 19 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4x\\le 12 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/7d/7d7303c5608dbd17911794959438f925d7ab6edd3ebba600d657b396ccf8eaa9.png)\n\nThen, we solve $6x+8<2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+8 & <2 \\\\ 6x & <-6 \\\\ x & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ad/ad5692ee92c2b67f50c0354020642bd9c711bdf7b88f4d476455512e33f9fc5f.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/63/638b44af1e33b78102a0dbfa3857c1292f200e026f54adf92fe77a97bf7e10a1.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/id #uuid "2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" "answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" "answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" "answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" "answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" :answer/id #uuid "fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/24/2463e5d528a3af7798456523c4e456c102ee3fb07828cd5680180d75bb27d2fd.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer/id #uuid "23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/63/638b44af1e33b78102a0dbfa3857c1292f200e026f54adf92fe77a97bf7e10a1.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" :answer/id #uuid "45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/7d/7d7303c5608dbd17911794959438f925d7ab6edd3ebba600d657b396ccf8eaa9.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" :answer/id #uuid "d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/a6/a63dd45bee5f32ae88bbb8fbfc274def0539794cfc3b1e88a34a42583832ef43.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019" :answer/id #uuid "982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019" :answer/type :answer.type/image :answer/value "images/ad/ad5692ee92c2b67f50c0354020642bd9c711bdf7b88f4d476455512e33f9fc5f.png" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186125027 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186059638 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/id #uuid "7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22036" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a36fe195458e459aea993232a72ed21e0c780135dc4dbe4bece45bfc3b6e50e2.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $50+25\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg." :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=50+25\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 50+25\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 25(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 25(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 25\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 25 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $25.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-063ce151-0ba3-5c75-910b-b7e2c256e6ec"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-063ce151-0ba3-5c75-910b-b7e2c256e6ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "063ce151-0ba3-5c75-910b-b7e2c256e6ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" "answer-2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" "answer-a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" "answer-015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" "answer-29d41b66-493d-5b0a-96b8-072a9c66c207"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer/id #uuid "ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" :answer/id #uuid "2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "25\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" :answer/id #uuid "a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" :answer/id #uuid "015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-29d41b66-493d-5b0a-96b8-072a9c66c207" :answer/id #uuid "29d41b66-493d-5b0a-96b8-072a9c66c207" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "50\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186054664 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a422bda1-83e5-5ea1-b276-7fb095067ffb"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a422bda1-83e5-5ea1-b276-7fb095067ffb" :question/id #uuid "a422bda1-83e5-5ea1-b276-7fb095067ffb" :question/math-academy-id "q-78760" :question/problem "![](images/61/612a4d26c399f754318b7aceb2bb0f329cf9515ea49a7da0d84d5d4aa1b672ea.png)\n\nUsing the graphical method, find the solutions $(x,y)$ of the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y &=-5 \\\\ y &=-{x}^{2}+4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The solutions $(x,y)$ of the system correspond to the intersection points of the two curves.\n\n![](images/6d/6d9da50ac2c05ae16125d48ed96e5a7a7ed1dbc03ddb53e96ab301d502abb17f.png)\n\nWe see from the graph that the curves intersect at \n\n$\\,$ $(-3,-5)\\,$ and $\\,(3,-5).$ \n\nTherefore, these are the solutions of the corresponding system." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-70c3d0a0-cfc9-5368-8e0e-665d3b3527ab"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-70c3d0a0-cfc9-5368-8e0e-665d3b3527ab" :answer-field/id #uuid "70c3d0a0-cfc9-5368-8e0e-665d3b3527ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-8c967535-4ab0-58a8-a729-8bc0b2f84aea" :answer-field/choices ["answer-228618c5-7982-5340-bbbe-5a5309961ca7" "answer-1c832b98-50f0-54df-a19b-b731f40d7b8f" "answer-9600d968-3c28-5e90-826a-fb2d658d24fb" "answer-8c967535-4ab0-58a8-a729-8bc0b2f84aea" "answer-61f21a8c-0f7f-5782-adc3-cc79fe53c3e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-228618c5-7982-5340-bbbe-5a5309961ca7" :answer/id #uuid "228618c5-7982-5340-bbbe-5a5309961ca7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,-5)$ and $(2,-5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c832b98-50f0-54df-a19b-b731f40d7b8f" :answer/id #uuid "1c832b98-50f0-54df-a19b-b731f40d7b8f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,-5)$ and $(4,-5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9600d968-3c28-5e90-826a-fb2d658d24fb" :answer/id #uuid "9600d968-3c28-5e90-826a-fb2d658d24fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-2,0)$ and $(2,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8c967535-4ab0-58a8-a729-8bc0b2f84aea" :answer/id #uuid "8c967535-4ab0-58a8-a729-8bc0b2f84aea" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,-5)$ and $(3,-5)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-61f21a8c-0f7f-5782-adc3-cc79fe53c3e1" :answer/id #uuid "61f21a8c-0f7f-5782-adc3-cc79fe53c3e1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$(-3,0)$ and $(3,0)$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186233141 :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7c0bdd98-1734-5283-bd19-3a50cb6e8817"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7c0bdd98-1734-5283-bd19-3a50cb6e8817" :answer-field/id #uuid "7c0bdd98-1734-5283-bd19-3a50cb6e8817" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-69f8f087-b4ab-539a-a92a-71c2b7e860e7" :answer-field/choices ["answer-4be48e3e-1c40-52d4-a265-9d0205cf8f91" "answer-1814fbcd-9f92-515e-9828-c49eef2bbaf2" "answer-5731e481-0681-52ab-b6b9-e017c2f03b1a" "answer-69f8f087-b4ab-539a-a92a-71c2b7e860e7" "answer-9e4a93a5-5f1b-534c-a5dc-2740ee32a078"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4be48e3e-1c40-52d4-a265-9d0205cf8f91" :answer/id #uuid "4be48e3e-1c40-52d4-a265-9d0205cf8f91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1814fbcd-9f92-515e-9828-c49eef2bbaf2" :answer/id #uuid "1814fbcd-9f92-515e-9828-c49eef2bbaf2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5731e481-0681-52ab-b6b9-e017c2f03b1a" :answer/id #uuid "5731e481-0681-52ab-b6b9-e017c2f03b1a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-69f8f087-b4ab-539a-a92a-71c2b7e860e7" :answer/id #uuid "69f8f087-b4ab-539a-a92a-71c2b7e860e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "43" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9e4a93a5-5f1b-534c-a5dc-2740ee32a078" :answer/id #uuid "9e4a93a5-5f1b-534c-a5dc-2740ee32a078" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "53" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087710 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-7f25e8cf-a84e-5491-8095-e34846bd72c0"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-7f25e8cf-a84e-5491-8095-e34846bd72c0" :question/id #uuid "7f25e8cf-a84e-5491-8095-e34846bd72c0" :question/math-academy-id "q-109613" :question/problem "Write $y=\\frac{1}{5}x+2$ in standard form." :question/worked-solution "Our goal is to write the equation in the form $ax+by=c,$ where $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors and $a\\ge 0.$\n\nWe begin by moving all of the variables to the left-hand side and all of the constants to the right-hand side. This gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{5}x+y=2\n$$\n\nNow, we multiply both sides of the equation by $-1:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{5}x+y & =2 \\\\ (-1)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{5}x+y) & =(-1)\\cdot (2) \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}x-y & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we multiply both sides of the equation by $5:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}x-y & =-2 \\\\ 5\\cdot (\\frac{1}{5}x-y) & =5\\cdot (-2) \\\\ x-5y & =-10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, $a,b,$ and $c$ are integers with no common factors, and $a\\ge 0.$ So we are done!\n\nThe standard form of the line is $x-5y=-10.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dad8335d-f4a7-566b-a578-6ac7a63c8d7b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dad8335d-f4a7-566b-a578-6ac7a63c8d7b" :answer-field/id #uuid "dad8335d-f4a7-566b-a578-6ac7a63c8d7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-448eccfb-3c08-5bec-841b-585bee529c4e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-9061fc30-c374-57e8-aa75-804d2bbafc4a" "answer-fa2a9e76-21e6-55c2-8f02-1bd6cfa3e2c8" "answer-bd9e69fa-90c3-5ff9-b4f9-43eaf28f779f" "answer-448eccfb-3c08-5bec-841b-585bee529c4e" "answer-60d77254-fa6e-530c-8178-4237af50304a"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9061fc30-c374-57e8-aa75-804d2bbafc4a" :answer/id #uuid "9061fc30-c374-57e8-aa75-804d2bbafc4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}x-y=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fa2a9e76-21e6-55c2-8f02-1bd6cfa3e2c8" :answer/id #uuid "fa2a9e76-21e6-55c2-8f02-1bd6cfa3e2c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x+5y=5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd9e69fa-90c3-5ff9-b4f9-43eaf28f779f" :answer/id #uuid "bd9e69fa-90c3-5ff9-b4f9-43eaf28f779f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5y+10=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-448eccfb-3c08-5bec-841b-585bee529c4e" :answer/id #uuid "448eccfb-3c08-5bec-841b-585bee529c4e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x-5y=-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-60d77254-fa6e-530c-8178-4237af50304a" :answer/id #uuid "60d77254-fa6e-530c-8178-4237af50304a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=5y-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186083191 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-745d6485-4fab-5db3-ad5a-442675f1d8d6"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-745d6485-4fab-5db3-ad5a-442675f1d8d6" :question/id #uuid "745d6485-4fab-5db3-ad5a-442675f1d8d6" :question/math-academy-id "q-3682" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a32739957ef5ff1bf81f49b1b1baaaab69c6ef3d2613f8ac09ad4020c91c50f7.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the curve shown above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $y=|x-h|+k$ is a vertical translation of the absolute value graph $y=|x|$ by $h$ units right and $k$ units up.\n\nHere, the graph is moved left by $4$ units and down by $1$ unit. This corresponds to $h=-4$ and $k=-1.$ So, the equation of the graph is $y=|x+4|-1.$\n\n![](images/fc/fcaf6e4e5e5fa63724be00a344c725e8bc9095c74c8b1114a0dbe90e9ac31935.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-ea40d3ec-5a65-5f11-9245-74d21f7dd219"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-ea40d3ec-5a65-5f11-9245-74d21f7dd219" :answer-field/id #uuid "ea40d3ec-5a65-5f11-9245-74d21f7dd219" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3cfff7a7-330b-572e-90cb-b9b5dddb8228" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d81edf6b-b7ac-5848-8692-2e21c1530fbc" "answer-42b5a490-0ee5-549d-8703-5b5cf81273db" "answer-3cfff7a7-330b-572e-90cb-b9b5dddb8228" "answer-13486019-a392-57be-a337-f52f79477f44" "answer-a91352d6-0efc-5355-a4fa-9b60746ec3f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d81edf6b-b7ac-5848-8692-2e21c1530fbc" :answer/id #uuid "d81edf6b-b7ac-5848-8692-2e21c1530fbc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=|x+1|-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-42b5a490-0ee5-549d-8703-5b5cf81273db" :answer/id #uuid "42b5a490-0ee5-549d-8703-5b5cf81273db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=|x+4|+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3cfff7a7-330b-572e-90cb-b9b5dddb8228" :answer/id #uuid "3cfff7a7-330b-572e-90cb-b9b5dddb8228" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=|x+4|-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-13486019-a392-57be-a337-f52f79477f44" :answer/id #uuid "13486019-a392-57be-a337-f52f79477f44" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=|x-1|-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a91352d6-0efc-5355-a4fa-9b60746ec3f8" :answer/id #uuid "a91352d6-0efc-5355-a4fa-9b60746ec3f8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "y=|x-4|-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186152110 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-1ac9a15a-91b5-5333-bd21-1c4aeb66e1dd"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-1ac9a15a-91b5-5333-bd21-1c4aeb66e1dd" :question/id #uuid "1ac9a15a-91b5-5333-bd21-1c4aeb66e1dd" :question/math-academy-id "q-67953" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f021a38a2c0c2098c14b2af479a609e85f6903ec84b4eafc71cb599becee3d9.png)\n\nWhich of the graphs above represent proportional relationships?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the graph of a proportional relationship is always a straight line that passes through the origin $(0,0).$\n\nOf the given graphs, only graph III fits this description.\n\n- Graph I is not a straight line.\n\n- Graphs II and IV do not pass through the origin $(0,0).$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\"." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-75afd0e8-6c0a-5237-becc-83e629f28d7f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-75afd0e8-6c0a-5237-becc-83e629f28d7f" :answer-field/id #uuid "75afd0e8-6c0a-5237-becc-83e629f28d7f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1fab5eef-9775-58f4-b57d-cb792b17ff32" :answer-field/choices ["answer-d7cfb344-0165-53cc-9422-4c18679479dc" "answer-5ff222c4-39ce-5121-9b09-72ad59c1f29e" "answer-3630b97b-56be-52b8-9178-cb1d3166fdf2" "answer-1fab5eef-9775-58f4-b57d-cb792b17ff32" "answer-10690335-5930-5fef-a862-6eb8da552d97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-d7cfb344-0165-53cc-9422-4c18679479dc" :answer/id #uuid "d7cfb344-0165-53cc-9422-4c18679479dc" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5ff222c4-39ce-5121-9b09-72ad59c1f29e" :answer/id #uuid "5ff222c4-39ce-5121-9b09-72ad59c1f29e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3630b97b-56be-52b8-9178-cb1d3166fdf2" :answer/id #uuid "3630b97b-56be-52b8-9178-cb1d3166fdf2" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II, III and IV only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1fab5eef-9775-58f4-b57d-cb792b17ff32" :answer/id #uuid "1fab5eef-9775-58f4-b57d-cb792b17ff32" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-10690335-5930-5fef-a862-6eb8da552d97" :answer/id #uuid "10690335-5930-5fef-a862-6eb8da552d97" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "None" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-f499a51b-0375-5fe9-adef-ba2c3ffe0ed5" :activity/id #uuid "f499a51b-0375-5fe9-adef-ba2c3ffe0ed5" :activity/title "Quiz 26" :activity/type :activity.type/assessment :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-6db8f8da-3b17-52a5-b393-3a58b8181d61" "step-eb1c4e40-39c2-5f5c-b2b6-26650419156e" "step-1786b470-22a1-5126-81ff-d7683858760a" "step-6efa7e92-f016-53bb-834a-4b1eccb1ced4" "step-76250baa-d726-5448-99de-f65c8294e71c" "step-f0ded8a3-36ee-53e7-9a9e-da01def8fc81" "