step/validate]} {:db/id "step-cd22f88a-3842-5752-b5b5-8be1505b996e" :step/id #uuid "cd22f88a-3842-5752-b5b5-8be1505b996e" :step/content 17592186233141 :step/next "step-7842a897-31cc-5300-9462-5bab9938e676" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-7842a897-31cc-5300-9462-5bab9938e676" :step/id #uuid "7842a897-31cc-5300-9462-5bab9938e676" :step/content "question-7f25e8cf-a84e-5491-8095-e34846bd72c0" :step/next "step-18997cdd-4144-5716-af59-75b7831d1856" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-18997cdd-4144-5716-af59-75b7831d1856" :step/id #uuid "18997cdd-4144-5716-af59-75b7831d1856" :step/content "question-745d6485-4fab-5db3-ad5a-442675f1d8d6" :step/next "step-24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :step/id #uuid "24fa352b-f67b-509b-9a54-bff1759f7275" :step/content "question-1ac9a15a-91b5-5333-bd21-1c4aeb66e1dd" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/id #uuid "e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/math-academy-id "q-225260"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/problem "**Fully** factor the following trinomial.\n\n$-12{a}^{2}-6a+6=$\n{{field-1}}$(a\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$)($\n{{field-3}}\n$a\\,-1)$"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/worked-solution "We need to factor the following expression:\n\n$$\n-12{a}^{2}-6a+6\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that all the terms have a common factor of $-6.$ So, we can simplify the calculation by first factoring out $-6:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6(2{a}^{2}+a-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we just need to factor the trinomial $2{a}^{2}+a-1$ in parentheses. To do this, we find two numbers that \n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant (which is $2\\times (-1)=-2$), and\n\n- add to the linear coefficient (which is $1$).\n\nThe factor pairs of $-2$ are\n\n$$\n(1,-2),\\,(-1,2).\n$$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-1,2)$ add to $1:$ \n\n$$\n-1+2=1\\,✓\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-a+2a,$ and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{a}^{2}+a-1 & = \\\\ 2{a}^{2}-a+2a-1 & = \\\\ (2{a}^{2}-a)+(2a-1) & = \\\\ a(2a-1)+(2a-1) & = \\\\ (a+1)(2a-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original trinomial factors as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-12{a}^{2}-6a+6 & = \\\\ -6(2{a}^{2}+a-1) & = \\\\ -6(a+1)(2a-1) & \\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/id #uuid "1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6"] ["answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer/id #uuid "b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790"] ["answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790" :answer/value "-6"] ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/correct "answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790"] ["answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6" :answer-field/choices "answer-b980c429-3941-5497-9718-eff2d9e2f790"] ["answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/id #uuid "417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044"] ["answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer/id #uuid "592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745"] ["answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/key "field-2"] ["answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/correct "answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745"] ["answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044" :answer-field/choices "answer-592954bd-e4e3-532e-b6ca-f2133054c745"] ["answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/id #uuid "97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864"] ["answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer/id #uuid "fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15"] ["answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/key "field-3"] ["answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/correct "answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15"] ["answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864" :answer-field/choices "answer-fc2978a6-8ff8-5d5b-8005-22bef1697c15"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-1743a921-81e3-55b5-9d48-3a7a62d7fca6"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-417b571f-db4b-5ef9-8922-9b03f5302044"] ["question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-97e49246-be20-50e1-b49e-21fb6572d864"] [17592186203943 :knowledge-point/questions "question-e8fb1410-51ee-5a0a-9a08-61072eaa2e45"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/id #uuid "03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/math-academy-id "q-338386"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/problem "Find the **exact** value of the limit.\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}}=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/worked-solution "Applying the root rule, we get\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\sqrt{(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} & =\\sqrt{{lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{({lim}_{x\\to 0}(3{x}^{2}+6x+9))}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(3(0)^{2}+6(0)+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0+0+9)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{9}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{729} \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/id #uuid "b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23"] ["answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer/id #uuid "fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01"] ["answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01" :answer/value "27"] ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/correct "answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01"] ["answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23" :answer-field/choices "answer-fcc5bc51-ebe5-5f7b-8b5e-1457adb75f01"] ["question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b99fd557-903d-52f2-b885-ba116704ea23"] [17592186054604 :knowledge-point/questions "question-03d1d0b4-f385-5136-a615-f2e1e9fef632"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/id #uuid "7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/math-academy-id "q-76083"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/problem "What is the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $3\\le 4x+7\\le 19$ or $6x+8<2?$"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/worked-solution "We start by solving $3\\le 4x+7\\le 19:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3 & \\le 4x+7\\le 19 \\\\ -4 & \\le 4x\\le 12 \\\\ -1 & \\le x\\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/7d/7d7303c5608dbd17911794959438f925d7ab6edd3ebba600d657b396ccf8eaa9.png)\n\nThen, we solve $6x+8<2:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+8 & <2 \\\\ 6x & <-6 \\\\ x & <-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](images/ad/ad5692ee92c2b67f50c0354020642bd9c711bdf7b88f4d476455512e33f9fc5f.png)\n\nTo graph the values of $x$ that satisfy either inequality, we overlay the two graphs on the same number line:\n\n![](images/63/638b44af1e33b78102a0dbfa3857c1292f200e026f54adf92fe77a97bf7e10a1.png)\n\nTherefore, the final solution is $x\\le 3.$"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/id #uuid "2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90"] ["answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" :answer/id #uuid "fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50"] ["answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50" :answer/value "images/24/2463e5d528a3af7798456523c4e456c102ee3fb07828cd5680180d75bb27d2fd.png"] ["answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer/id #uuid "23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f"] ["answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f" :answer/value "images/63/638b44af1e33b78102a0dbfa3857c1292f200e026f54adf92fe77a97bf7e10a1.png"] ["answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" :answer/id #uuid "45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3"] ["answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3" :answer/value "images/7d/7d7303c5608dbd17911794959438f925d7ab6edd3ebba600d657b396ccf8eaa9.png"] ["answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" :answer/id #uuid "d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104"] ["answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104" :answer/value "images/a6/a63dd45bee5f32ae88bbb8fbfc274def0539794cfc3b1e88a34a42583832ef43.png"] ["answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019" :answer/id #uuid "982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019"] ["answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019" :answer/type :answer.type/image] ["answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019" :answer/value "images/ad/ad5692ee92c2b67f50c0354020642bd9c711bdf7b88f4d476455512e33f9fc5f.png"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/correct "answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/choices "answer-fad71dcb-4bdd-5e5e-9ebe-bbb5c3d95d50"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/choices "answer-23f86dbc-d003-51d1-827e-f13bf7fdff1f"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/choices "answer-45465aa1-5e0a-5908-b63c-595a84123bb3"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/choices "answer-d5ac308f-1478-5136-85b9-dc1b3ab87104"] ["answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90" :answer-field/choices "answer-982998cd-20b3-5f6f-b36c-446e47274019"] ["question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-2baf93f4-97eb-565b-8259-f33d93d8df90"] [17592186115323 :knowledge-point/questions "question-7c7074e0-f02c-5273-a98a-de3d3f3ee6a7"] [17592186125027 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/id #uuid "7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a"] ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-22036"] ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/problem "![](images/a3/a36fe195458e459aea993232a72ed21e0c780135dc4dbe4bece45bfc3b6e50e2.png)\n\nThe perimeter of the above triangle is $50+25\\sqrt{2}.$ Find the measure of each leg."] ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/worked-solution "Because the triangle is isosceles, the legs must have the same length. Let $a$ be the length of each leg. So, we have\n\n$$\nAB=BC=a.\n$$\n\nMoreover, because the triangle is a *right* isosceles triangle, the hypotenuse must be equal to $\\sqrt{2}$ times the length of a leg. Therefore,\n\n$$\nAC=AB\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=a\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, since the perimeter is $p=50+25\\sqrt{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =AB+BC+AC \\\\ 50+25\\sqrt{2} & =a+a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 25(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =2a+a\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 25(2+\\sqrt{2}) & =(2+\\sqrt{2})a \\\\ 25\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})} & =\\cancel{(2+\\sqrt{2})}a \\\\ 25 & =a\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the measure of a leg is $25.$"] ["question-7002a70c-d40e-53ed-9d27-c94492760a6a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-063ce151-0ba3-5c75-910b-b7e2c256e6ec" :answer-field/id #uuid "063ce151-0ba3-5c75-910b-b7e2c256e6ec"] ["answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer/id #uuid "ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2"] ["answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ad072040-2706-54b1-aafe-7b97f68a33a2" :answer/value "25"] ["answer-2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" :answer/id #uuid "2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9"] ["answer-2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2272b44c-dbba-5930-a68e-ca0f3289afd9" :answer/value "25\\sqrt{2}"] ["answer-a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" :answer/id #uuid "a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68"] ["answer-a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a30e18e9-8725-50fa-90c2-6a03a46e5e68" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" :answer/id #uuid "015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48"] ["answer-015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-015e29d4-44ac-5ca8-a43f-99ecdd54ff48" :answer/value "50"] ["answer-29d41b66-493d-5b0a-96b8-072a9c66c207" :answer/id #uuid "29d41b66-493d-5b0a-96b8-072